    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0079" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg70"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">138 Emergency Program/759a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-03-25T17:00:00-05:00">March 25, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. With reference to the Department’s telegrams of November 17, 6 p.m. and
                    November 22, 6 p.m., 1939,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d58-f1"/> the Department desires
                    that no passport be validated for the journey through the combat zone of the
                    North Atlantic en route to the United States without permission being first
                    obtained from the Department.</p>
                <p>Please so inform offices in Europe.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
